prompt.en:
A developer writes a recursive function that resolves a new Promise on each call and chains `.then` to loop:
```js
function loop(n) {
  if (n <= 0) return;
  Promise.resolve().then(() => loop(n - 1));
}
loop(1_000_000);
```
Which statement best explains what happens to the event loop while this runs?

